From 306f148f0d4f15e813c2ab6724add71d9e26b9a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fred Horch <fred.horch@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:37:54 -0400
Subject: Always open an explicitly requested command-line file

Omawrite 0.5.0 starts the QML editor before inspecting argv.  The blank
editor can mark the backend modified during startup, which made the old
`!backend.modified()` guard skip Backend::open() altogether.  As a result,
`omawrite /path/to/plan.md` displayed an empty Untitled.md window.

An explicit file argument is an instruction to replace any recovered or
transient blank document, so it must take precedence over that state.

Retires when upstream includes this change (or an equivalent) in 0.5.1+.

(Patch carried in ~/pkgs by Fred's Omarchy workstation; registry: https://github.com/greenermoose/omarchy-fred-ecosystem)

AI-Tool: claude 2.1.274
AI-Model: Claude Opus 5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/main.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index 8b222132b3f7d01be02015db0fe9daf27d20ef3d..7e0dcac0ed311bf741e1475784145536419797b4 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -72,7 +72,7 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
     backend.setParentWindow(qobject_cast<QWindow *>(engine.rootObjects().constFirst()));
 
     const QStringList args = app.arguments();
-    if (args.size() > 1 && !backend.modified())
+    if (args.size() > 1)
         backend.open(QUrl::fromLocalFile(args.at(1)));
 
     return app.exec();
